d at taking criticism (adaptability), can be unorganized (reliability). So strengths strong, but concerns moderate.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Concerns: can be grumpy, can be uncooperative (crew cooperation, communication). So reliability and stress good, but cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), known to be 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere with crew (crew cooperation). Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (crew cooperation), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong reliability and decision, but communication and adaptability issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: regarded as arrogant (crew cooperation), relatively weak leadership skills (leadership). So good technical, responsibility, but cooperation issues.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Candidate A has strong leadership and technical, but unorganized and poor at criticism. Candidate B reliable and stress but uncooperative. Candidate C reliable and decision, but communication and egocentric. Candidate D strong problem solving and responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate A because leadership and anticipation are critical for long-distance, and unorganized may be mitigated; but inability to take criticism could be risk. Candidate B's uncooperative may be serious. Candidate C's egocentric and communication issues could affect crew. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership also problematic.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate A as leading, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion (none) but can say \"Given we have not yet discussed, I will start by proposing...\"\n\nMake sure to include at least one fact per candidate? Not required, but need evidence.\n\nWe'll state recommendation Candidate A.\n\nNow produce output."}
